# Scoped Trivy allowlist — review and prune when upstream ships a fix.
#
# supercronic v0.2.49 (latest, published 2026-08-14) ships a binary built with
# Go stdlib 1.26.6, which carries these FIXABLE HIGH CVEs:
#   CVE-2026-78667  net/http  DoS via crafted HTTP Range headers  (fixed in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2)
#   CVE-2026-97031  crypto/tls DoS via multiple ECH outer extension refs (fixed in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2)
#   CVE-2026-78669  net/http HTTP/2 CPU DoS via repeated initial-window settings (fixed in Go 1.26.9/1.27.2)
# Advisory: https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6611 (published 2026-10-08).
# These are denial-of-service, not RCE. In this image supercronic only runs the
# local cron that execs the Python sync — no HTTP listener (no
# -prometheus-listen-address). Managed cron clears inherited SENTRY_DSN,
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT and SENTRY_RELEASE before both supercronic invocations,
# preventing its optional Sentry HTTP client. Python performs broker HTTP.
# These exceptions apply only to the managed entrypoint, without command or
# entrypoint overrides. Reassess before enabling Go network features.
# Checked upstream 2026-10-10: no rebuilt release yet (v0.2.49 is latest).
#
# Remove these lines once supercronic publishes a release built with Go >= 1.26.9.
# Re-review by: 2026-11-15
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-78669
